<title>UK: Black, Baltic Sea oil exports fall 370k bpd on wee.</title>
<headline>Black, Baltic Sea oil exports fall 370k bpd on wee.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil exports from Baltic and Black Sea terminals fell 370,252 barrels a day (bpd) to 1.4 million bpd in the first week of February from the previous week but were little changed from the same week last year, Petro-Logistics said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude exports from Baltic and Black Sea ports fell 372,465 bpd on the week to 866,134 bpd. This represented a rise of 10,444 bpd over the same period last year.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports fell 22,685 bpd to 366,816 bpd and included 38,525 bpd from Romania and Bulgaria.</p>
<p>Heavy fuel exports rose 15,343 bpd to 163,737 bpd and were 95,566 bpd higher than last year.</p>
<p>Gasoline and jet exports combined were 576 bpd lower on the week at 26,135 bpd but higher by 26,135 bpd over the same period last year.</p>
